The optical-flow interpolation is a derivative of Futatabi, which is part of
Nageru:

  Copyright (C) 2018 Steinar H. Gunderson
  https://nageru.sesse.net/

Futatabi implements a GPU version of:

  Till Kroeger, Radu Timofte, Dengxin Dai and Luc Van Gool,
  "Fast Optical Flow using Dense Inverse Search", ECCV 2016.

The occlusion-aware blend follows the temporal-interpolation method Futatabi
uses, which is based on occlusion reasoning for frame interpolation with
optical flow. Ported sources under src/flow keep that attribution in their
headers.

The WebRTC preview (1.4.0) adapts code by the same author from:

  mxl-webrtc-monitor (https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-webrtc-monitor), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Adrian Hilber: the MediaMTX child supervisor
  (src/ops/child.cpp) and the MediaMTX configuration (src/ops/preview.cpp).
  mxl-multiviewer (https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-multiviewer), Apache License 2.0:
  the H.264 publisher, the preview settings checks and the widget origin check.
  FlowXer engine prototype (https://github.com/Firesh0ot/FlowXer), Apache License
  2.0: NVENC on CUDA frames in the process's own context.

The container image bundles MediaMTX (https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx),
MIT License, as a separate program; its licence is in
/usr/share/doc/mediamtx/LICENSE in the image.
